      "author": "Hollowmere team",
      "story": "The Larch Hollow mill ran a night shift to the last, cutting the logs the camps had already decked. When the Hollowed came up from the pond the crew barred the big doors from inside and climbed to the lunchroom; the watchman's log keeps the times. Kowalski went down for the fuses and did not come up, so they barricaded the basement stairs below. The office with the payroll could only be reached through the basement now, and the filer kept its key on his board by the grinder. Near five in the morning Gus, the night watchman, started the headsaw to draw them off the lunchroom. The saw is quiet now. Something still walks on the log deck, and down in the basement they lie in the sawdust like they are sleeping.",
